# Pixel Cosmos rules for Cline

Follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) and start with
[documentation/README.md](documentation/README.md).

- Treat `documentation/` as source documentation and `docs/` as generated
  output.
- Preserve seed determinism. Use the project RNG/hash helpers and stable IDs;
  never use `Math.random()` for generated gameplay or economic results.
- Store only mutable save deltas. Rebuild baseline systems, markets and
  catalogues from seed.
- Create a new item instance with `makeItem()` whenever an item is purchased,
  installed, looted or moved into cargo.
- Use the shared ship renderer. Hull render configuration belongs to the hull
  instance.
- Put visible text in Russian and English locale files, and make unavailable
  actions explain why.
- Keep game rules in `src/game/`, keep scenes thin, and test deterministic
  behaviour with same-seed tests.
- Verify with focused `npm.cmd test -- ...` and `npx.cmd vite build`.

Detailed references: [scanner/economy](documentation/gameplay/SCANNER_AND_ECONOMY.md),
[mechanics](documentation/gameplay/GAME_MECHANICS.md),
[scanner design](documentation/design/SCAN_DESIGN.md),
[economy plan](documentation/plans/ECONOMY_ROADMAP.md), and
[shipyard render contract](documentation/design/PIXEL_SHIPYARD_JSON_SPEC.md).
